+## 1. Declaration of AI Assistance
+
+In strict compliance with academic integrity guidelines and Section 17 (Item 10) of the project specification, this record accurately describes the substantial role of AI assistance in RouteBudget Lab. AI assistance was **not** limited to high-level brainstorming; it actively participated across code implementation, test development, statistical analysis, debugging, and technical documentation:
+
+### 1.1 Architecture & Code Implementation
+- **C++ Resumable Engine & Partial Acceptance:**
+  - AI assisted in designing and implementing the `computeOptimisticUpperBound` 64-bit checked arithmetic filter in `src/engine/rbl_partial_acceptance.cpp`.
+  - AI assisted in implementing the bounded checkpoint store eviction hook (`attemptEvictionRecovery`) and terminal reserve recovery hook (`attemptTerminalRecovery`) in `src/engine/rbl_resumable_engine.cpp`.
+  - AI assisted in extending the command-line profiler (`src/profiler/profile_partial_acceptance.cpp`) to support the 5 matched selective policies and terminal-reserve control.
+
+### 1.2 Automated Test Engineering
+- **Section 11 / 12 Correctness Suites:**
+  - AI assisted in authoring the 22-category automated test suite in `tests/selective_recovery_tests.cpp`.
+  - AI implemented the test assertion macros (`ASSERT_EQ`, `ASSERT_TRUE`, `ASSERT_FALSE`) that remain active under `-O3 -DNDEBUG`, and verified them via intentional failure injection.
+  - AI developed edge-case tests including cyclic dependencies, duplicate agent rejection, 64-bit arithmetic overflow detection, and deadline boundary cutoffs.
+
+### 1.3 Experimental Scripts & Statistical Analysis
+- **Automation & Statistical Pipelines:**
+  - AI authored the cyclic Latin-square balanced benchmark runner `scripts/run_selective_recovery_pilot.py`.
+  - AI authored the statistical analysis script `scripts/analyze_selective_recovery.py`, implementing exact two-sided binomial sign tests, Wilcoxon signed-rank tests, clustered instance aggregation, high-resolution timing breakdowns, and opportunity funnel accounting.
+
+### 1.4 Technical Documentation & Review
+- AI assisted in drafting, reviewing, and auditing the technical reports, correction ledger (`docs/correction_ledger.md`), requirements-to-tests matrix (`docs/requirements_to_tests_matrix.md`), decisions log (`docs/decisions.md`), and research log (`docs/research-log.md`).
+- All empirical claims, numerical tables, and statistical results were programmatically generated from actual C++ execution outputs and raw JSON telemetry files on the author's local machine.
